## CP00 — Objects, conventions and exact mathematical suppliers

Let Σ be a smooth oriented Hausdorff second-countable three-manifold without boundary. For the uniform Sobolev theorem take Σ=T³=R³/(2πZ)³; for the local smooth geometric theorem allow any such Σ and a potentially point-dependent neighborhood. M is a neighborhood of {0}×Σ with Lorentz metric g of signature −+++, future normal n with g(n,n)=−1 and four-volume orientation vol_g=ds∧vol_h initially. s=x⁰ is a length coordinate. Curvature is R(X,Y)Z=∇X∇YZ−∇Y∇XZ−∇[X,Y]Z, Ric_bd=R^a_bad. K(X,Y)=g(∇Xn,Y), hence K=½L_nh, agreeing with GR E2. F is a real antisymmetric covariant tensor, a section of Λ²T*M. The metric Hodge dual is (*F)_ab=½ε_abcdF^cd. In an oriented orthonormal slice tetrad (n,e_i), write e_i=F(e_i,n), b_i=½ε_i{}^{jk}F(e_j,e_k). Thus F(n,e_i)=−e_i and F(e_i,e_j)=ε_ijkb_k. The letter e for electric components is distinct from the tetrad vector e_i where its argument is displayed. In SI e=E/c and b=B. Maxwell is dF=0 and d*F=μ₀i_jvol_g, equivalently ∇_aF^{ab}=−μ₀j^b. Source-free means j=0. Constants κ=8πG_N/c⁴>0, μ₀>0 and Λ∈R are fixed.

Set Q_ab(F,g)=F_acF_b{}^c−¼g_abF_cdF^cd, T_EM=μ₀^−1Q. Define the mathematical electrovacuum system G_ab+Λg_ab=κT_EM, dF=d*F=0. Q is algebraic in (g,g^−1,F); it is not an arbitrarily stipulated source with independently adjustable components. A solution is a metric and two-form satisfying these equations classically in the stated regularity class. A development additionally has an initial embedding i:Σ→M, i* g=h, second fundamental form K and the specified electric/magnetic data; geometric equivalence is a time-orientation-preserving isometry fixing i and pulling back F (and any matter fields) to the corresponding fields.

Adopt AC as in GR E0's admitted integration/compactness interfaces. For integer s≥5, H^s(T³) is the real Fourier-coefficient completion with ||u||_s²=Σ_(k∈Z³)(1+|k|²)^s|û(k)|² and conjugation symmetry. The inspected published `thm-fourier-basis-and-parseval-on-the-n-torus` applies after period-one rescaling. Its weak derivative coefficient identity identifies this with integer weak-derivative Sobolev spaces. GR E0's fully read argument supplies embeddings H^s→C^j for s−j>3/2, product/chain estimates at s≥5, finite Fourier Galerkin approximation with variable positive time matrix, compact C_tH^(s−1) convergence, energy uniqueness/stability and common-interval smooth persistence. Its exact theorem is: for smooth symmetric matrices A^μ(t,x,U), smooth B on a finite-dimensional open admissible state set, uniformly positive A⁰ on compact state neighborhoods, initial U₀∈H^s with values in such a neighborhood, A⁰U_t+A^iU_i+B=0 has a unique local solution U∈L∞H^s∩CH^(s−1), U_t∈L∞H^(s−1), with bounded-set common time and CH^(s−1) stability; smooth data persist smoothly on that same local time. The choice of s≥5 deliberately avoids endpoint analytic estimates. CP04 below verifies every coefficient hypothesis and every new principal block rather than replacing the theorem by a generic existence reference.

Proof status: GR E0–E3, G0–G4 and H0–H4 are completed research arguments, not published item receipts. E0 is reused as a pure mathematical local supplier. Root PDE/Fourier/FA plans permit the interfaces but are not themselves proofs; E0 gives the actually consumed estimates and construction. External Friedrich–Rendall pp24–33 was read in full; its printed mollifier formula and composition estimate are not used without correction (source dispositions record why).

