## CP02 — Initial constraints and explicit harmonic data (mathematics)

Data are (h,K,e,b): positive symmetric spatial metric h, symmetric K, and spatial vector fields e,b, with h used to lower spatial indices and choose vol_h/cross product. Their Maxwell constraints are D_ie^i=0 and D_ib^i=0. This follows because the initial pullbacks of *F and F are i_evol_h and i_bvol_h, respectively; exterior derivative is divergence times vol_h. The Einstein constraints are
R(h)+(tr_hK)²−|K|_h²=2Λ+(κ/μ₀)(|e|_h²+|b|_h²),
D^jK_ji−D_i tr_hK=−(κ/μ₀)(e×_h b)_i.
GR E2's point-normal Gauss/Codazzi proof was read in full: Γ⁰_ij=K_ij and Γ^i_0j=K^i_j yield R^g_ijkl=R^h_ijkl+K_ikK_jl−K_ilK_jk; taking the appropriate Lorentz traces gives twice G(n,n), and the mixed contraction gives Ric_0i=D^jK_ji−D_i trK. Substitution of CP01's actual stress, rather than a separately prescribed density/flux, gives exactly the above constraints. Their smoothness orders suffice for the high-Sobolev data below; weak assertions are not substituted for classical equations.

For H^(s+1) h, H^s K,e,b on T³, s≥5, assume a uniform positive lower bound for h and impose these equalities as Sobolev/classical equalities (embeddings make all the displayed terms continuous). Define initial spacetime g_ij=h_ij,g_00=−1,g_0i=0 and ∂_sg_ij=2K_ij. Fix a **smooth** positive reference metric γ, background bar g=−ds²+γ, and harmonic-map vector H^a=g^bc(Γ^a_bc−barΓ^a_bc). Set Q^i=h^jk(Γ(h)^i_jk−Γ(γ)^i_jk), ∂_sg_0i=h_ijQ^j, ∂_sg_00=−2tr_hK. Then initial H⁰=½∂_sg_00+trK=0 and H^i=Q^i−h^ij∂_sg_0j=0. These are direct contractions of the Christoffel formula. Q∈H^s by inverse/composition/product estimates, so all initial metric first derivatives belong to H^s. When h is smooth one may choose γ=h and obtain GR E2's ∂_sg_0i=0. At finite regularity using bar g=−ds²+h would violate E0's hypothesis that prescribed coefficient functions in x are smooth; the fixed-reference construction repairs that assigned consumer without editing the earlier source.

Initial F is reconstructed uniquely by F(n,e_i)=−e_i and F(e_i,e_j)=ε_ijkb_k. This algebraic map uses h and its positive square roots for a smooth local slice frame; it has the same H^s regularity. No time derivatives of F are freely specified: CP03's first-order evolution determines them. The initial lapse is one and shift zero, but their time derivatives are chosen by harmonic gauge; they are not independently fixed functions thereafter.

