## CP06 — Controlled charged barotropic Einstein–Maxwell–fluid branch (mathematics)

Let ε range in an open interval J, p(ε) smooth, ε+p>0 and 0<p'(ε)<1 throughout the selected compact state interval. Let u be a future unit timelike velocity, parametrized locally by its three spatial components on the unit hyperboloid; let N_*>0 and ε_*∈J. Define N(ε)=N_*exp(∫_(ε*)^ε dz/(z+p(z))) and an advected scalar Z. Set j=cN(ε)Z u and T_m=(ε+p)u♭⊗u♭+pg. The matter equations are ∇^aT_m,ab=F_bcj^c and u(Z)=0; u's normalization is built into its local coordinates. Source-free electrovacuum is a separate branch, not this sourced one.

Contracting the matter balance with u gives u(ε)+(ε+p)div u=0 because u^bF_bcj^c=cNZ u^bF_bcu^c=0 by skewness. Differentiating the displayed N gives u(N)+Ndiv u=0. Therefore ∇_aj^a=cZ∇(Nu)+cNu(Z)=0 exactly. No independently assigned current or assumed continuity law is smuggled in. The orthogonal projection of matter momentum is (ε+p)∇_uu_b+h_b{}^a∂_ap=F_bcj^c, h_b{}^a=δ_b{}^a+u_bu^a. Its force is smooth algebraic in (g,F,ε,u,Z) and vanishes in the u contraction.

Define r(ε)=∫_(ε*)^ε√(p'(z))/(z+p(z))dz, a smooth invertible state coordinate, c_s=√p'∈(0,1). In local rest-space coordinates for variations tangent to u's hyperboloid, the principal r/u symbol is [[ζ(u),c_sζ_perpᵀ],[c_sζ_perp,ζ(u)I₃]]. This is precisely GR E3's explicitly checked fluid reduction. The extra Z equation has symbol ζ(u) and no derivative of r or u; choose Z as the independent variable, **not charge density q**, since q's continuity equation would contain div u in its principal part. The full block is symmetric and positive for a future-positive timelike ζ because ζ(u)>|ζ_perp| and c_s<1. Connection/metric first derivatives and the Lorentz force are lower-order variables already present in CP04. Stress and current are algebraic in these state variables. Adding this block to the Einstein/Maxwell blocks therefore meets E0's smooth coefficient/positive time hypotheses on compact states away from enthalpy/sound-speed degeneracy and velocity-chart boundaries.

Sourced Maxwell evolution is i_n dF=0 and i_n(d*F−μ₀i_jvol_g)=0. All new source components are algebraic j values. Let V=d*F−μ₀i_jvol_g; then i_nV=0 and dV=−μ₀(div j)vol_g=0 by the just-proved fluid equations. CP03's scalar residual transport proves full sourced Maxwell constraints propagate. CP01 gives div T_EM=−Fj, while the matter equations give div T_m=+Fj; total stress is conserved. CP04's Einstein subsidiary proof applies to T_EM+T_m, including its nonzero trace. The reduced Einstein right side is κ(T_total−½tr(T_total)g)+Λg. There is thus a complete local high-Sobolev/smooth and smooth-geometric-uniqueness theorem for compatible data in this strict interior model. Initial Gauss is D_ie^i=−μ₀g(j,n), D_ib^i=0, and gravitational constraints use T_total(n,n),T_total(n,e_i). On-shell conservation and the residual transport supply all previously required coupled premises. Physical sound speed is cc_s.

N(ε) is an EOS-defined positive density, not a claim that every EOS has a microscopic particle derivation. Its normalization N_* is additional model data; in physical use N is particle number per volume and Z charge per particle. No pressureless dust, shocks, vacuum/free boundary, degeneracy p'=0, p'≥1, arbitrary prescribed charged current, dissipative conducting fluid, Vlasov continuum or point charge is included. A scalar/current appended without its own conservation/symmetric reduction would not be covered by this proof.

