## CP07 — Worked data, obstructions, scales and conditional physical use

For Λ=0 on flat T³, e=b=0,K=0 satisfies all four constraints and Minkowski g=−ds²+δdx², F=0 is the exact development. For nonzero constant parallel e,b, choose K=Hh with H²=κ(|e|²+|b|²)/(6μ₀). Then trK=3H, |K|²=3H², so the Hamiltonian side is 6H² and the Maxwell/Gauss and momentum constraints vanish (e×b=0). CP04 gives a genuine nontrivial smooth electrovacuum development. It is not asserted spatially isotropic at later times: the initial electromagnetic stress is anisotropic. By contrast, flat h,K=0,Λ=0 and any nonzero e or b fail the Hamiltonian constraint; a nonzero smooth EM field on a fixed Minkowski background is a test-field model, not a sourceful Einstein–Maxwell solution.

If a spatial two-cycle has a nonzero magnetic period, the initial F sector need not admit a global A. Uniform b normal to one coordinate torus gives an explicit nonzero period. CP03/CP04 use the two-form and thus retain this sector. In the charged-fluid branch on compact Σ without boundary, integrate Gauss: 0=∫div_h e=−μ₀∫g(j,n). Thus the total normal charge is zero; uniform one-sign nonzero charged matter data are incompatible on the torus. This is an exact compatibility obstruction, not a measured cosmological conclusion. The EOS p=wε, ε>0,0<w<1 has N=N_*(ε/ε_*)^(1/(1+w)), r=(√w/(1+w))log(ε/ε_*), so invertibility, positive enthalpy and strict subluminality are explicit. Set Z=0 for its neutral sector; nonzero Z still requires solving the displayed Gauss and gravitational constraints.

SI units in x⁰=ct coordinates: g dimensionless; h dimensionless coordinate components; K,Q^i,H^a 1/m; connection 1/m; curvature,Λ 1/m²; F,e,b Tesla; E V/m=c·Tesla; A Tesla·m; j A/m²; T,ε,p Pa=J/m³; μ₀ N/A²; κ m/J; c m/s; G_N m³/(kg·s²). Fluid u,n are dimensionless, N m^−3,Z coulomb, cNZ u A/m². r is dimensionless, N_* a primitive normalization. All coordinate component units transform with charts; a frame is a chosen tetrad or adapted chart, not a change in physical dimensions. Metric, electromagnetic field and matter initial data are primitive fields of the adopted model; induced h,K,e,b,current,stress and gauge vector are derived by the displayed maps. c,G_N,μ₀,Λ,EOS and N_* are model parameters; ε₀=(μ₀c²)^−1, sound speed and geometrized field below are derived.

For standard geometrized exact-solution normalization put mathcal F=√(κ/(2μ₀))F. It has 1/m units because (κ/μ₀)F² has 1/m². Then Einstein electrovacuum is Ric_ab−Λg_ab=2[mathcal F_ac mathcal F_b{}^c−¼g_ab mathcal F²]. Source-free Maxwell is unchanged by this constant rescaling. This specifies the factor of two needed to compare Reissner–Nordström/Kerr–Newman conventions; geometrized charge and SI charge still require the exact solution's flux normalization.

Under `post-emg-einstein-maxwell-action` and `def-emg-geometry-units`, the stationarity/model equations are the just-defined SI Einstein–Maxwell system. Conditional physical theorems consume CP04/CP05 for local model evolution and CP01–CP04 for conservation and constraint propagation. For the charged-fluid physical theorem, adopt `post-emg-einstein-maxwell-equations` (the coordinator's explicit equation-based model postulate) together with `post-emg-strict-charged-fluid-model`. The first postulate supplies Einstein and sourced Maxwell equations with the actual total stress; the second supplies exactly CP06's matter stress/EOS/current/advection laws. CP06 establishes the compatible local development, current and total-stress conservation, and all constraint/gauge subsidiaries for those equations. Therefore the conditional physical conclusion follows without asserting a fluid matter functional or using an arbitrary-matter action premise. The electrovacuum Sm=0 branch and CP09's actually constructed scalar-action branch retain `post-emg-einstein-maxwell-action`. No observations are used. Mathematical validity of the developments does not prove applicability of classical GR/EM or their constitutive matter branch to nature.

