## CP09 — Classical charged complex scalar branch with a complete first-order reduction

This branch uses a globally specified real one-form A and hence initial magnetic two-form **exact** in its selected trivial-potential sector. It is distinct from the nonexact electrovacuum sectors of CP07. Let complex φ be dimensionless, K_φ>0 [J/m], λ∈R [(Tesla·m²)^−1], and V:an open interval→R smooth with V(|φ|²) [m^−2]. No Planck constant is used. Define D_aφ=∂_aφ−iλA_aφ, π_a=D_aφ. The adopted classical scalar action is S_φ=−K_φ/(2c)∫[g^ab Re(π_a*π_b)+V(|φ|²)]vol_g. Compactly supported variations in the two real components give D^aD_aφ−V'(|φ|²)φ=0. To verify, vary π, integrate the gauge-covariant pairing by parts (the imaginary connection terms cancel under Re), and use δV=2V'Re(φ*δφ). Variation in A gives j^a=K_φλ Im(φ*π^a): δπ_a=−iλφδA_a, δ|π|²=−2λ Im(φ*π^a)δA_a, so δS_φ=c^−1∫j^aδA_a. Combined with the electromagnetic action this gives ∇_aF^{ab}=−μ₀j^b. Metric variation gives T_φ,ab=K_φRe(π_a*π_b)−(K_φ/2)g_ab(|π|²+V); vary g^ab and δvol=−½g_abδg^abvol to check all factors. Maxwell stress remains CP01's tensor.

Gauge is A→A+dχ, φ→exp(iλχ)φ, π→exp(iλχ)π, χ [Tesla·m²]. Differentiating the phase verifies D'φ'=exp(iλχ)Dφ, so the scalar action, stress and current are invariant. On shell current conservation is exact: ∇_aj^a=K_φλ Im[(D_aφ)*D^aφ+φ*D^aD_aφ]=0, since the first contraction and V'|φ|² are real. Also [D_a,D_b]φ=−iλF_abφ. Differentiating T and using the scalar equation cancels the potential terms, leaving K_φRe(π^{a*}(D_aπ_b−D_bπ_a))=K_φλ Im(π^{a*}φ)F_ab=F_baj^a. Thus div(T_EM+T_φ)=0 after Maxwell holds, with the same source sign as CP01.

**Precise evolution variables and principal equations.** Impose temporal potential gauge A₀=0 in the length-time coordinate and evolve A_i,s=F₀i. Evolve φ_s=π₀. Treat π₀,π_i as independent complex variables (two real components each) with
∂_sπ_i−∂_iπ₀=−iλA_iπ₀−iλF₀iφ,
and D^aπ_a=V'(|φ|²)φ,
where gauge-covariant differentiation of a covector is ∂_aπ_b−Γ^c_abπ_c−iλA_aπ_b. Use the first displayed equations in the divergence equation: its leading terms are g⁰⁰∂_sπ₀+2g⁰i∂_iπ₀+g^ij∂_iπ_j, precisely the same positive symmetric wave reduction as the metric block. Connection/A/commutator terms are algebraic in (g,∂g,A,F,φ,π), and no derivative of A or F appears in this scalar principal block. The φ and A_i equations are positive-time transport blocks. Append these and the sourced CP03 Maxwell block to CP04's metric block. The combined matrices are block symmetric, positive on the same small-shift metric neighborhood, and all coefficients are smooth functions of the finite-dimensional variables. E0 applies at s≥5 to metric h H^(s+1), K H^s, F/A/π H^s and φ H^(s+1), with uniform compact admissibility. Initial potential consistency is F_ij=∂_iA_j−∂_jA_i and π_i=∂_iφ−iλA_iφ; π_n is the independently specified scalar normal derivative. Einstein/Maxwell constraints use the actual total stress and current.

**Sequential subsidiaries, without potential-wave Ricci coupling.** First C_i=π_i−∂_iφ+iλA_iφ has ∂_sC_i=0: substitute the explicit π_i,φ,A_i evolution equations and cancel ∂_iπ₀, A_iπ₀ and F₀iφ term by term. Initial C=0 gives π=Dφ. Magnetic dF=0 propagates by CP03 independently of current conservation. Then ∂_s(∂_iA_j−∂_jA_i−F_ij)=∂_iF₀j−∂_jF₀i−∂_sF_ij=0 by the (0,i,j) closedness component. Initial potential consistency therefore gives F=dA. The evolved scalar divergence is now the actual scalar equation, so the just-proved current conservation holds. Sourced Maxwell error V=d*F−μ₀i_jvol is spatial with dV=−μ₀divj vol=0, hence its initial Gauss constraint propagates by the same scalar normal transport. Full Maxwell now gives total-stress conservation, and CP04's Bianchi wave forces Einstein harmonic H=0. The metric derivative constraints are unchanged. This completes local high-Sobolev and smooth Einstein–Maxwell–charged-scalar evolution in the stated potential sector, with no missing matter/gauge subsidiary.

Smooth local geometric uniqueness is up to isometry **and electromagnetic gauge** fixing the initial potential/scalar data. CP05's harmonic comparison diffeomorphisms may destroy A₀=0; restore it by solving ∂_sχ=−A₀ with χ initially zero. The solution is the time integral of the smooth coefficient, with no spatial elliptic or Ricci equation. Transform φ,π by the corresponding phase; their initial covariant data are unchanged. The resulting reduced initial states coincide, so E0 uniqueness gives equality and the original developments are related by the comparison isometry and gauge. No rough geometric-uniqueness strengthening is asserted. In this branch the source-free MGHD theorem CP08 is not silently reused as a gauge-bundle global theorem.

The real/imaginary parts of φ are classical fields, not quantum amplitudes. λ is a chosen classical coupling scale independent of ℏ; K_φ and V are independent constitutive/action parameters. Neither sign/size of V nor a special polynomial degree is needed locally on compact states. The simple φ=0 branch with V(0)=0 and π=0 has j=T_φ=0, hence every CP04 electrovacuum solution admitting its selected potential is an exact zero-scalar solution. With λ=0 the current vanishes identically and the two real scalars are neutral; this is a controlled reduction, not a charged-particle or quantum-field assertion. Arbitrary nontrivial U(1) bundles, singular currents and optimal weak solution thresholds require their own separate developments.

All Sobolev estimates are applied after fixing positive reference length L₀ and field scale F₀ and replacing coordinates by X/L₀ and first derivatives/fields by L₀v,L₀w,e/F₀,b/F₀ (and fixed matter scales). Constant invertible rescalings act by congruence on symmetric principal matrices and preserve positive time weights. This reconciles dimensionless Fourier coefficient norms with the SI component conventions. Maxwell residual scalar q,r in CP03 have Tesla/m units; gauge χ has Tesla·m² units. Fixed scales are bookkeeping parameters, not new physical laws.
